<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1599">1599</a>–<a href="/years/1785">1785</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ashtarkhanids, Toqay-Timurids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Janids, also called Ashtarkhanids, were a Chinggisid dynasty that ruled the Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> from 1599 to 1785. Descended from the khans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astrakhan">Astrakhan</a>, they succeeded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaybanids">Shaybanids</a>, to whom they were linked by marriage. Their realm lost lands to its neighbours, became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> in 1740 and fell under the control of the Manghit chiefs, who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Bukhara.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Janid dynasty" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Musavvir · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Imamquli-khan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
